      "name": "Lone Wolf",
      "created_at": "2024-08-26T06:19:52.461Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hello,</p>\n<p>I am working on Provident Fund(PF) module development in ERPNext v.15. My CTO shared with me many documents and sample forms. Here is on of the sample form of PF module,</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/3/a/3a00df3d0dbd9680b752e667b444654874d2f342.png\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/3a00df3d0dbd9680b752e667b444654874d2f342\" title=\"PF_SS\"><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/3/a/3a00df3d0dbd9680b752e667b444654874d2f342_2_690x294.png\" alt=\"PF_SS\" data-base62-sha1=\"8h7yOL2q6tN5Ueo1wD0UJ1O67xo\" width=\"690\" height=\"294\" srcset=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/3/a/3a00df3d0dbd9680b752e667b444654874d2f342_2_690x294.png, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/3/a/3a00df3d0dbd9680b752e667b444654874d2f342_2_1035x441.png 1.5x, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/3/a/3a00df3d0dbd9680b752e667b444654874d2f342_2_1380x588.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"DFE4EA\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">PF_SS</span><span class=\"informations\">1738×743 65.7 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>\n<p>I explained the child table design and structure in Frappe to my CTO and demonstrated how we could display sample form table data in our child table. Afterward, he was disappointed and said, ‘<strong>Why does an advanced web application framework like Frappe have such a limitation, only allowing us to show 10 columns of data in a child table, rather than displaying it like the sample form table?</strong>’</p>\n<p>I couldn’t respond effectively. Is Frappe have any plan to restructure the child table design to overcome these limitations?</p>",
